  "goodToKnow": "Kitschig means kitschy, tacky or overly sentimental: ein kitschiger Sonnenuntergang, kitschige Deko. Der Kitsch is one of the German words English borrowed, probably from Munich art dealers in the 1870s. Classic examples are Gartenzwerge (garden gnomes) and Schneekugeln (snow globes). A soppy song or film is a Schnulze. Some people love Kitsch ironically."
